.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
CPP-API: The \fBImporter\fP class forms an C++ interface to the functionality of the Open Asset Import Library\&.
.PP
Create an object of this class and call \fBReadFile()\fP to import a file\&. If the import succeeds, the function returns a pointer to the imported data\&. The data remains property of the object, it is intended to be accessed read-only\&. The imported data will be destroyed along with the \fBImporter\fP object\&. If the import fails, \fBReadFile()\fP returns a nullptr pointer\&. In this case you can retrieve a human-readable error description be calling \fBGetErrorString()\fP\&. You can call \fBReadFile()\fP multiple times with a single \fBImporter\fP instance\&. Actually, constructing \fBImporter\fP objects involves quite many allocations and may take some time, so it's better to reuse them as often as possible\&.
.PP
If you need the \fBImporter\fP to do custom file handling to access the files, implement \fBIOSystem\fP and \fBIOStream\fP and supply an instance of your custom \fBIOSystem\fP implementation by calling \fBSetIOHandler()\fP before calling \fBReadFile()\fP\&. If you do not assign a custion IO handler, a default handler using the standard C++ IO logic will be used\&.
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
One \fBImporter\fP instance is not thread-safe\&. If you use multiple threads for loading, each thread should maintain its own \fBImporter\fP instance\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SH "Constructor & Destructor Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "Assimp::Importer::Importer ()"
Constructor\&. Creates an empty importer object\&.
.PP
Call \fBReadFile()\fP to start the import process\&. The configuration property table is initially empty\&. 
.SS "Assimp::Importer::Importer (const \fBImporter\fP & other)\fR [delete]\fP"
Copy constructor\&.
.PP
This copies the configuration properties of another \fBImporter\fP\&. If this \fBImporter\fP owns a scene it won't be copied\&. Call \fBReadFile()\fP to start the import process\&. 
.SS "Assimp::Importer::~Importer ()"
Destructor\&. The object kept ownership of the imported data, which now will be destroyed along with the object\&. 
.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "const \fBaiScene\fP * Assimp::Importer::ApplyCustomizedPostProcessing (BaseProcess * rootProcess, bool requestValidation)"

.SS "const \fBaiScene\fP * Assimp::Importer::ApplyPostProcessing (unsigned int pFlags)"
Apply post-processing to an already-imported scene\&.
.PP
This is strictly equivalent to calling \fBReadFile()\fP with the same flags\&. However, you can use this separate function to inspect the imported scene first to fine-tune your post-processing setup\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpFlags\fP Provide a bitwise combination of the \fBaiPostProcessSteps\fP flags\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A pointer to the post-processed data\&. This is still the same as the pointer returned by \fBReadFile()\fP\&. However, if post-processing fails, the scene could now be nullptr\&. That's quite a rare case, post processing steps are not really designed to 'fail'\&. To be exact, the #aiProcess_ValidateDS flag is currently the only post processing step which can actually cause the scene to be reset to nullptr\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
The method does nothing if no scene is currently bound to the \fBImporter\fP instance\&. 
.br
 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBvoid\fP Assimp::Importer::FreeScene ()"
Frees the current scene\&.
.PP
The function does nothing if no scene has previously been read via \fBReadFile()\fP\&. \fBFreeScene()\fP is called automatically by the destructor and \fBReadFile()\fP itself\&. 
.br
 
.SS "const char * Assimp::Importer::GetErrorString () const"
Returns an error description of an error that occurred in \fBReadFile()\fP\&.
.PP
Returns an empty string if no error occurred\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A description of the last error, an empty string if no error occurred\&. The string is never nullptr\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
The returned function remains valid until one of the following methods is called: \fBReadFile()\fP, \fBFreeScene()\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "const std::exception_ptr & Assimp::Importer::GetException () const"
Returns an exception if one occurred during import\&.
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The last exception which occurred\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
The returned value remains valid until one of the following methods is called: \fBReadFile()\fP, \fBFreeScene()\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBvoid\fP Assimp::Importer::GetExtensionList (\fBaiString\fP & szOut) const"
Get a full list of all file extensions supported by ASSIMP\&.
.PP
If a file extension is contained in the list this does of course not mean that ASSIMP is able to load all files with this extension --- it simply means there is an importer loaded which claims to handle files with this file extension\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIszOut\fP String to receive the extension list\&. Format of the list: '*\&.3ds;*\&.obj;*\&.dae'\&. This is useful for use with the WinAPI call GetOpenFileName(Ex)\&. 
.RE
.PP

