.SS "\fBIOSystem\fP * Assimp::Importer::GetIOHandler () const"
Retrieves the IO handler that is currently set\&. You can use \fBIsDefaultIOHandler()\fP to check whether the returned interface is the default IO handler provided by ASSIMP\&. The default handler is active as long the application doesn't supply its own custom IO handler via \fBSetIOHandler()\fP\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A valid \fBIOSystem\fP interface, never nullptr\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBvoid\fP Assimp::Importer::GetMemoryRequirements (\fBaiMemoryInfo\fP & in) const"
Returns the storage allocated by ASSIMP to hold the scene data in memory\&.
.PP
This refers to the currently loaded file, see \fBReadFile()\fP\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIin\fP Data structure to be filled\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
The returned memory statistics refer to the actual size of the use data of the \fBaiScene\fP\&. Heap-related overhead is (naturally) not included\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBaiScene\fP * Assimp::Importer::GetOrphanedScene ()"
Returns the scene loaded by the last successful call to \fBReadFile()\fP and releases the scene from the ownership of the \fBImporter\fP instance\&. The application is now responsible for deleting the scene\&. Any further calls to \fBGetScene()\fP or \fBGetOrphanedScene()\fP will return nullptr - until a new scene has been loaded via \fBReadFile()\fP\&.
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Current scene or nullptr if there is currently no scene loaded 
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Use this method with maximal caution, and only if you have to\&. By design, \fBaiScene\fP's are exclusively maintained, allocated and deallocated by \fBAssimp\fP and no one else\&. The reasoning behind this is the golden rule that deallocations should always be done by the module that did the original allocation because heaps are not necessarily shared\&. \fBGetOrphanedScene()\fP enforces you to delete the returned scene by yourself, but this will only be fine if and only if you're using the same heap as assimp\&. On Windows, it's typically fine provided everything is linked against the multithreaded-dll version of the runtime library\&. It will work as well for static linkage with \fBAssimp\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBProgressHandler\fP * Assimp::Importer::GetProgressHandler () const"
Retrieves the progress handler that is currently set\&. You can use \fBIsDefaultProgressHandler()\fP to check whether the returned interface is the default handler provided by ASSIMP\&. The default handler is active as long the application doesn't supply its own custom handler via \fBSetProgressHandler()\fP\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A valid \fBProgressHandler\fP interface, never nullptr\&. 
.RE
.PP

