.SS "const \fBaiScene\fP * Assimp::Importer::ReadFile (const char * pFile, unsigned int pFlags)"
Reads the given file and returns its contents if successful\&.
.PP
If the call succeeds, the contents of the file are returned as a pointer to an \fBaiScene\fP object\&. The returned data is intended to be read-only, the importer object keeps ownership of the data and will destroy it upon destruction\&. If the import fails, nullptr is returned\&. A human-readable error description can be retrieved by calling \fBGetErrorString()\fP\&. The previous scene will be deleted during this call\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpFile\fP Path and filename to the file to be imported\&. 
.br
\fIpFlags\fP Optional post processing steps to be executed after a successful import\&. Provide a bitwise combination of the \fBaiPostProcessSteps\fP flags\&. If you wish to inspect the imported scene first in order to fine-tune your post-processing setup, consider to use \fBApplyPostProcessing()\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A pointer to the imported data, nullptr if the import failed\&. The pointer to the scene remains in possession of the \fBImporter\fP instance\&. Use \fBGetOrphanedScene()\fP to take ownership of it\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
\fBAssimp\fP is able to determine the file format of a file automatically\&. 
.RE
.PP

