.SS "const \fBaiScene\fP * Assimp::Importer::ReadFileFromMemory (const \fBvoid\fP * pBuffer, size_t pLength, unsigned int pFlags, const char * pHint = \fR''\fP)"
Reads the given file from a memory buffer and returns its contents if successful\&.
.PP
If the call succeeds, the contents of the file are returned as a pointer to an \fBaiScene\fP object\&. The returned data is intended to be read-only, the importer object keeps ownership of the data and will destroy it upon destruction\&. If the import fails, nullptr is returned\&. A human-readable error description can be retrieved by calling \fBGetErrorString()\fP\&. The previous scene will be deleted during this call\&. Calling this method doesn't affect the active \fBIOSystem\fP\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpBuffer\fP Pointer to the file data 
.br
\fIpLength\fP Length of pBuffer, in bytes 
.br
\fIpFlags\fP Optional post processing steps to be executed after a successful import\&. Provide a bitwise combination of the \fBaiPostProcessSteps\fP flags\&. If you wish to inspect the imported scene first in order to fine-tune your post-processing setup, consider to use \fBApplyPostProcessing()\fP\&. 
.br
\fIpHint\fP An additional hint to the library\&. If this is a non empty string, the library looks for a loader to support the file extension specified by pHint and passes the file to the first matching loader\&. If this loader is unable to completely the request, the library continues and tries to determine the file format on its own, a task that may or may not be successful\&. Check the return value, and you'll know \&.\&.\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A pointer to the imported data, nullptr if the import failed\&. The pointer to the scene remains in possession of the \fBImporter\fP instance\&. Use \fBGetOrphanedScene()\fP to take ownership of it\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
This is a straightforward way to decode models from memory buffers, but it doesn't handle model formats that spread their data across multiple files or even directories\&. Examples include OBJ or MD3, which outsource parts of their material info into external scripts\&. If you need full functionality, provide a custom \fBIOSystem\fP to make \fBAssimp\fP find these files and use the regular \fBReadFile()\fP API\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBaiReturn\fP Assimp::Importer::RegisterLoader (\fBBaseImporter\fP * pImp)"
Registers a new loader\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpImp\fP \fBImporter\fP to be added\&. The \fBImporter\fP instance takes ownership of the pointer, so it will be automatically deleted with the \fBImporter\fP instance\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
AI_SUCCESS if the loader has been added\&. The registration fails if there is already a loader for a specific file extension\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBaiReturn\fP Assimp::Importer::RegisterPPStep (BaseProcess * pImp)"
Registers a new post-process step\&.
.PP
At the moment, there's a small limitation: new post processing steps are added to end of the list, or in other words, executed last, after all built-in steps\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpImp\fP Post-process step to be added\&. The \fBImporter\fP instance takes ownership of the pointer, so it will be automatically deleted with the \fBImporter\fP instance\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
AI_SUCCESS if the step has been added correctly\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBvoid\fP Assimp::Importer::SetExtraVerbose (bool bDo)"
Enables 'extra verbose' mode\&.
.PP
'Extra verbose' means the data structure is validated after \fIevery\fP single post processing step to make sure everyone modifies the data structure in a well-defined manner\&. This is a debug feature and not intended for use in production environments\&. 
.SS "\fBvoid\fP Assimp::Importer::SetIOHandler (\fBIOSystem\fP * pIOHandler)"
Supplies a custom IO handler to the importer to use to open and access files\&. If you need the importer to use custom IO logic to access the files, you need to provide a custom implementation of \fBIOSystem\fP and IOFile to the importer\&. Then create an instance of your custom \fBIOSystem\fP implementation and supply it by this function\&.
.PP
The \fBImporter\fP takes ownership of the object and will destroy it afterwards\&. The previously assigned handler will be deleted\&. Pass nullptr to take again ownership of your \fBIOSystem\fP and reset \fBAssimp\fP to use its default implementation\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpIOHandler\fP The IO handler to be used in all file accesses of the \fBImporter\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBvoid\fP Assimp::Importer::SetProgressHandler (\fBProgressHandler\fP * pHandler)"
Supplies a custom progress handler to the importer\&. This interface exposes an #Update() callback, which is called more or less periodically (please don't sue us if it isn't as periodically as you'd like it to have \&.\&.\&.)\&. This can be used to implement progress bars and loading timeouts\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpHandler\fP Progress callback interface\&. Pass nullptr to disable progress reporting\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Progress handlers can be used to abort the loading at almost any time\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "bool Assimp::Importer::SetPropertyBool (const char * szName, bool value)\fR [inline]\fP"
Set a boolean configuration property\&. Boolean properties are stored on the integer stack internally so it's possible to set them via \fBSetPropertyBool\fP and query them with \fBGetPropertyBool\fP and vice versa\&. 
.PP
